\DOC SIMPS_TAC

\TYPE {SIMPS_TAC : thm list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Simplify the goal with the simp set and some more theorems.

\DESCRIBE
{SIMPS_TAC thl} simplifies the goal with the rules that have been
declared with {add_simp} and the theorems of {thl}. It is {CONV_TAC
(SIMPS_CONV thl)}, so it solves the goal where the simplification reaches
{true}.

To simplify with the assumptions of the goal as well, use
{ASM_SIMPS_TAC}.

\FAILURE
Fails if the goal cannot be simplified.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # g `count (Call (Cons (Num 3) Nil)) = 1`;;
  # e (SIMPS_TAC [ADD_CLAUSES]);;
  val it : goalstack = No subgoals
}

\SEEALSO
add_simp, ASM_SIMPS_TAC, SIMP_TAC, SIMPS_CONV, SIMPS_RULE.

\ENDDOC
